{
  "about": "A public call reads each file it is given by the language header it declares (SCHEMA-2, SCHEMA-4, LAYER-2, LAYER-4, PROJECT-1). The engine reads language 1.0 (#3030 D76): it refuses a newer version, and a file that declares schema_version, which is language 0.5 with yamaa beside it or not, as unsupported_language_version, and a file of another type as unexpected_file_type, each at the field that names the file: the entry's own yamaa or schema_version, a layer's parent (LAYER-4), a schema link (input.<name>.schema), a project's listing (<section>.specs[i]) or the project file's root, which names the project file as source and entry. A malformed header stays a finding in the file that declares it, as a layer's other findings do: a layer may leave out required fields, but a field it writes is checked and its keyed members are unique. Moved from declaration_language_header.rs, whose tests compared each issue's phase, condition, rule, spec paths and context, which compares names, or its whole row, span and operand route included; a test that read a few fields names those. A test that read an internal entry point (prepare_specification, check_references, document::decode) is a public check here: its rows add the phase and rule of each finding's cause, from the condition registry, and, for a finding in a layer, that layer as source and the entry as entry, which a check's refusal of a layer names. A listing that cannot be read has no name, so its cases find it by its index: a project check (listing_failure) and a project run (listing_step) report the same row for it, each naming the specification as its entry, and a submission that composes the section reports it without one, saving nothing.",
  "documents": {
    "spec": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: input.csv}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "legacy": "schema_version: '1.0'\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: input.csv}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "base": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ninput: {SRC: input.csv}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "child": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\nparent: base.yaml\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID]}\n",
    "listing_project": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: project\nsdtm:\n  specs: [dm.yaml, listed.yaml]\n",
    "submission_project": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: project\nstudy: {id: S, name: S, description: A study, protocol_name: S-01}\nsdtm:\n  specs: [listed.yaml]\n  standards: [{name: SDTMIG, version: \"3.4\", status: Final}]\n  define: define.xml\n"
  },
